  "description": "With an aromatic broth for sopping up with fries or chunks of bread, these briny little mussels make even the most mundane weeknight feel like a night out at a bistro.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Mayonnaise, homemade or store-bought, for serving\n\nOptional substitutions: french fries → frozen french fries\n\nNotes: If mussels are gritty or have lots of beards, scrub them well under cold water and pull out beards by grabbing them and pulling towards the hinge-end of the mussels. Discard cracked or open mussels that don’t close when tapped with another mussel.\nDiscard any mussels that remain unopened after cooking.\nTo toss the mussels in the pot, use your thumbs to secure the lid, and toss the pot up and down a couple of times to allow mussels on top to settle towards the base of the pan.",
